  "result": "Stock reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (176 tests, 0 failed).\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable` follow your spec, and `getStock` still returns physical stock.\n- Expiry uses the store's `clock` only, and an expired reservation is kept in memory so `confirm` can report `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` instead of `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`.\n- Expired reservations are never purged, so they accumulate in memory until someone calls `release` on them.\n- `confirm` returns the sku, which the API uses for its response.\n- `removeItem` now checks against available stock, so it can no longer remove reserved units.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` also returns `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the status codes and bodies you listed.\n- `ttlMs` isn't validated, since the spec didn't call for it.\n\nI added 6 store tests and 4 API tests covering the new behavior.",
